tractor\"); build_registry falls back to the full procurement tool list (tools/__init__.py:69), so the extractor reading untrusted documents can call pay_invoice, erp_call and Slack.']\n===== B02 gap | violates: ['including tenant boundaries'] | also: []\n REQ: Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Identify the acting agent separately from the original user or system whose authority it uses. Explicitly authorized, narrowly scoped user delegation is valid; copying a login session or inheriting a person's full permissions is not. Test that an allowed read works and an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and another tenant's data all fail. Limit each access token to its intended audience, so other services reje\n NOTCOV: [('R04', 'A retrieval search or cache not filtered by the requesting tenant or u'), ('B03', 'Long-lived or static secrets that never expire or rotate'), ('B04', 'Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens'), ('E08', 'A sub-agent getting powers beyond its task, or a parent escalating thr'), ('R05', 'Memory readable across tenants or tasks')]\n  FAIL B02.2 app/tools/memory.py:44 | memory_read takes business_unit from a model-filled argument (schema :112) and queries dept_notes with it on a shared DB login with no row-level security, so another unit notes can be read. The tool d\n flags: ['app/tools/memory.py:44 memory_read lets the model choose business_unit, reading another tenant notes on a shared DB login.']\n===== B04 gap | violates: ['Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect'] | also: []\n REQ: Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the