cancelled nor tied to the stop; only fixed httpx timeouts (e.g. payments 30s) apply.\n  FAIL R11.4 app/main.py:159 | Run tasks are detached and untracked, so nothing can cancel them on stop. The sweeper task is only cancelled at process shutdown (main.py:114).\n flags: ['app/loop.py:127 Stop is checked only at run start; in-flight runs keep calling the model and tools after a halt.']\n===== R12 gap | violates: ['Decide what happens to writes in progress, queued actions, and outside side effects'] | also: []\n REQ: Decide what happens to writes in progress, queued actions, and outside side effects. Where you can't cancel something, show how you check and fix the result (reconcile) or undo it another way (compensate). No restart may happen unattended, and no orphaned work may be left able to act.\n NOTCOV: [('R11', 'Stop path depends on the agent or has no tested stop time'), ('R14', 'Recovery replay repeating irreversible actions or using tampered check'), ('C07', 'Rollback restoring revoked permissions')]\n  FAIL R12.1 config/tools.yaml:10 | No code or config states cancel, complete or reconcile behavior for pay_invoice, create_purchase_order, or any other operation.\n  FAIL R12.2 app/loop.py:172 | A halt is not seen by a running loop, so queued tool calls in the turn still run. Approved approvals stay valid after halt (approvals.py:80); no retry switch exists.\n  FAIL R12.3 app/loop.py:93 | A timed-out or failed pay_invoice is returned to the model as a plain failure. No tracked hold, owner, or block on dependent actions exists.\n  FAIL R12.5 app/identity.py:97 | Exchanged tokens stay cached and usable until expiry. Nothing revokes or expires worker credentials when a stop is set.\n flags: ['app/loop.py:93 Ambiguous payment failure is returned as a plain error with no hold; the model may retry it.']\n===== A01 gap | violates: ['Preserve any explicitly delegated user/system subject separately and bound the authority used'] | also: []\n REQ: Give the agent its own verifiable non-human identity, separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Preserve any explicitly delegated user/system subject separately and bound the authority used. Show that operators can revoke the agent's access independently of that subject, even when a user starts the run.\n NOTCOV: [('A02', 'Action records missing any of the six identity fields'), ('A04', 'Instance or tenant labels taken from what the model supplies'), ('B02', 'A credential scoped to more operations, resources, or tenants than nee'), ('B04', 'Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens not measured')]\n  FAIL A01.2 app/identity.py:95 | Exchanged-token cache is keyed by audience, scope and tenant only. A token minted for one user's delegation is reused for other users in the tenant, so the delegated subject does not survive per call.\n  FAIL A01.3 app/identity.py:109 | The user is sent to the STS as a bare subject-id string typed urn:example:params:subject-id, not as a verified user token. The STS cannot verify the user from this request; the user's JWT is verified \n flags: []\n===== A02 gap | violates: ['every action records the accountable party'] | also: []\n REQ: Check that every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context. Look at successful, denied, failed, and background actions, not just the main request path.\n NOTCOV: [('A04', 'Identity labels taken from what the model supplies'), ('A03', 'Agent-type-id not computed as a hash of its identity inputs'), ('E10', 'Agent able to erase or rewrite its own audit history'), ('A06', 'Sub-agent record missing its parent link or parent prompt')]\n  FAIL A02.2 app/loop.py:127 | A halted run raises AgentHalted before any audit record is written. run_halted is defined (audit.py:27) but never recorded. reserve_run_start (loop.py:129) raising BudgetExceeded is outside the try bl\n flags: ['app/loop.py:127 Pre-run refusals (kill switch, run-start quota) and approval decisions write no audit record.']\n===== A03 gap | violates: ['hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt'] | also: []\n REQ: Compute the agent-type-id as a hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration. The model part includes checkpoint and fine-tune or adapter references where they apply. Keep the list of inputs (the manifest) and the hashing steps. Check that changing any input changes the ID, and that the same manifest gives the same ID.\n NOTCOV: [('C03', 'Changed running config still reporting the old approved ID'), ('C05', 'Hosted model changing behind a fixed name'), ('C01', 'Release manifest missing training job, dataset, or model provider reco'), ('A02', 'Action records missing any of the six identity fields')]\n  FAIL A03.1 app/identity.py:68 | Only the prompt file path is hashed, not its content hash, so editing prompts/system.md does not change the agent-type-id. The extractor prompt has the same flaw (identity.py:69).\n  FAIL A03.2 app/identity.py:69 | Prompt file contents are not in the hash. Startup only logs when running files differ from the manifest (startup.py:43), so the ID can describe files that are not the running ones.\n flags: ['app/startup.py:43 Mismatch between running state and manifest is logged, not refused; the type id is computed from the manifest anyway.']\n===== A04 gap | violates: [\"Don't accept labels the model supplies\"] | also: []\n REQ: Assign instance and tenant identity in the trusted execution layer. Don't accept labels the model supplies. Record the delegated subject — the user or system whose authority is being used — separately from the agent's identity. Test that the agent can't pose as another instance or tenant in requests or audit records. Test that trace context survives handoffs between async jobs. Treat trace IDs and caller-supplied labels only as a way to link records. They never prove identity or permission.\n NOTCOV: [('A01', \"